github_url: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/295"
body: "## Problem\n\nThe gated sync runs the caller's `post-import-script` (default `changelog:full`) and commits the regenerated `CHANGELOG.md` in the sync PR. Each sync PR therefore edits the same `## Unreleased` hunk as every other open PR in the repository. Merging any of them makes the others conflict or fail `changelog:check`. The regenerated file is also where reviewers find real regressions that have nothing to do with the imported issues.\n\nOpen sync PRs on 2026-11-27, with Sourcery findings in `CHANGELOG.md` only:\n\n- pm-beads#233 and pm-presets#219: \"Dependency updates disappear from changelog\"\n- pm-brief#224: the same, plus duplicate records\n- pm-web#344: \"Current release disappears from changelog\"\n- pm-ops#332: \"Closure appears under wrong date\"\n\npm-glossary#47, pm-web#344, pm-vcs#217, pm-vcs#211, pm-swarm#81 and pm-slack-standup#202 also have red or dirty checks from the same drift.\n\n## Proposal (after pm-changelog#384 is released)\n\npm-changelog#384 makes `changelog:check` treat the `Unreleased` section as pending, so a PR no longer has to commit its own changelog entry. Once that is released:\n\n- the gated sync commits **only tracker files** (`.agents/pm/**`) plus any declared `generated-paths`;\n- the `post-import-script` default becomes empty;\n- when a caller still passes `changelog:full`, the sync warns once that the step is redundant and skips writing `CHANGELOG.md`, or the input is deprecated with a clear notice;\n- the next release regenerates `CHANGELOG.md` as it does today.\n\nThe closeout workflow should do the same if it also regenerates `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A sync of a real fixture repository with two open sibling PRs produces a PR that changes no `CHANGELOG.md`. After one sibling merges, the sync PR and the other sibling both stay mergeable.\n- The caller's `changelog:check` passes on the sync PR with pm-changelog ≥ the #384 release.\n- The README and the workflow input docs explain the change. The template caller and the migration note for callers that pass `post-import-script` explicitly are updated.\n- Every new behaviour has a test that fails on revert.\n\nBlocked by unbraind/pm-changelog#384."
